  Device compatibility matrix: what the vendor image requires of the framework.

  Empty because the X-ROM x1 reference board has no vendor HALs that call into
  framework interfaces. This is a consequence of the Treble posture X-ROM takes
  rather than an omission: AVF, the isolation daemon and the Microdroid payload
  all live on the platform side (system / system_ext), so a generic system image
  can be flashed over this vendor image and everything X-ROM adds keeps working.

  When a vendor component does need a framework interface, add it here with the
  exact version range and optional="false". PRODUCT_ENFORCE_VINTF_MANIFEST
  (BoardConfig.mk section 7) turns an undeclared dependency into a build error.
-->
